{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrzdUZQ9xxLhT1QrWZHs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The version-specific pre-built handling is in place, and both test files pass (222 tests). I couldn't type-check or lint. mypy and ruff aren't installed in `.venv`, so I skipped `hatch run lint:fix` and the mypy check.\n\n**`_pbi.py`**\n- `is_pre_built(version)` and `get_wheel_server_url(version)` now strip the local segment with `Version(version.public)` before the version-specific lookup.\n- `is_pre_built(version)` calls the `is_pre_built` hook only when a version is given, through `overrides.find_and_invoke` with the new `_default_is_pre_built`. A non-None hook result wins over YAML.\n- The `pre_built` and `wheel_server_url` properties now call those methods with no version, so there is one code path.\n- The `versionadded` directives are bumped to 0.95.0, in `_models.py` as well.\n- `_models.py` already coerced a bare `versions:` key to an empty mapping, so I changed nothing there. `wheels.get_wheel_server_urls` already accepted `version`, so I left it alone too.\n\n**`_start.py`**\n- Added `_re_resolve_url(...)` as specified. For source packages, I pin the requirement to `name==version` and use `resolver.PYPI_SERVER_URL` as the sdist server, the same way `bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py` does.\n- The START phase now re-resolves the URL right after `pbi_pre_built` is set. It logs INFO before, uses the new URL on success, and logs a WARNING and keeps the old URL on `None`.\n- This runs before the graph update and the has-been-seen check, so a second parent of an already-seen package still gets its edge recorded.\n\n**Docs and tests**\n- I added a section on version-specific pre-built settings to `docs/concepts/package-settings.rst`. I also added a paragraph on the `is_pre_built` hook to `docs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst`.\n- New tests in `tests/test_packagesettings.py` cover local-version stripping, the properties not calling the hook, and a hook result overriding YAML. They also cover the default hook returning `None` and `versions:` being `None` or omitted.\n- New tests in `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py` cover when re-resolution triggers, the warning fallback on failure, and the already-seen case. They also cover `_re_resolve_url` for both the pre-built and source paths.\n- I updated the existing `test_sets_pbi_pre_built_before_prepare_source` mock. Its `get_wheel_server_url` would otherwise have differed from `wheel_server_url` and triggered a re-resolve."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11982,"cache_read_input_tokens":115593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11982},"output_tokens":750,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12d1b6e1-2731-4546-8651-45406c69c8d4","uuid":"5cc2ce6a-beef-4e65-8cb2-f2b8af6d5c7a","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:40:22.222Z","request_id":"req_011CfrzdUF3QFsUzx68vyMjA"}
